---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TestimonialCard from '../components/TestimonialCard.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
---

<Layout title="About — Udhaya Kumar" description="About Udhaya Kumar, Senior Backend Engineer with 13+ years building backend systems, data infrastructure, and production platforms.">
  <section style="padding: 52px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);">
    <h1 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: var(--fs-40); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 32px;">About</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 24px;">I've spent {profile.experience} building backend systems and data infrastructure. From {profile.convertCart.tenure}, I was at ConvertCart, where I owned a data platform end to end — ingestion, modelling, serving, and reporting — for {profile.convertCart.platformOwnership}. I helped grow the platform team from {profile.convertCart.teamGrowth} while serving {profile.proof.merchants}.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">I'm a {profile.primaryTitle} open to backend, platform, data infrastructure, technical lead, and founding-engineer roles across Indian, international, remote, and hybrid teams.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- What I get hired for -->
  <section style="padding: 52px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);">
    <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: var(--fs-32); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 40px;">What I get hired for</h2>
    <div style="display: grid; gap: 32px;">
      <div>
        <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Platform ownership</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">End-to-end responsibility for systems serving multiple internal teams and hundreds of external users. Comfortable holding both the design decisions and the operational debt. Own systems from architecture through production, incident response, and technical direction.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Design for reversibility</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">Ship simpler systems by deferring normalization to layers where mistakes are cheap to fix. Trade off one-time complexity at ingest for ongoing flexibility. Spend operations cost to buy reversibility.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Scaling with small teams</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">Scaled a platform team from 4 to 7 engineers while serving 200+ merchants across five commerce platforms. Focus on automation, clear ownership, and choosing the right abstractions so humans don't become the bottleneck.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Judging tradeoffs honestly</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">Every architecture decision trades something off. Value candidates and team members who name the cost admitted, not just the benefit gained. Leads to better hiring and fewer bad surprises post-launch.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Testimonials -->
  <section style="padding: 52px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);">
    <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: var(--fs-32); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 40px;">What people say</h2>
    <div style="display: grid; gap: 24px;">
      <TestimonialCard
        quote="I worked with Udhay for the past four years, and calling him just a 'team lead' wouldn't do justice to the role he played in my journey. He has been an exceptional mentor and guide, always approachable, patient, and supportive. His leadership style helped me grow not just in skills, but in confidence and mindset."
        name="Goutham Kishore"
        role="Full Stack Developer, reported to Udhaya"
      />
      <TestimonialCard
        quote="Udhaya is an exceptional engineer with strong technical depth and the curiosity to solve complex client challenges. He combines a high ownership mindset with excellent communication, translating technical concepts clearly for non-technical stakeholders. He approaches problems strategically and drives solutions with minimal oversight."
        name="Mannat Bhalla"
        role="Customer Success Manager"
      />
      <TestimonialCard
        quote="Udhaya has demonstrated an impressive ability to manage complex product development projects while leading a diverse team. His leadership style fosters a supportive environment where team members can thrive. He has effectively mentored colleagues and consistently ensures strong outcomes for both clients and the team."
        name="Vasudeva Sagari"
        role="Engineering Manager / Former Manager"
      />
      <TestimonialCard
        quote="Udhaya is an exceptional leader who sets high standards for his team and inspires them to reach their full potential. His technical expertise has been invaluable to the success of our projects. I believe that Udhaya would be an asset to any organization."
        name="Piyush Jaiswal"
        role="Backend Engineer, reported to Udhaya"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Engineering Principles -->
  <section style="padding: 52px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);">
    <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: var(--fs-32); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 40px;">Engineering Principles</h2>
    <div style="display: grid; gap: 32px;">
      <div>
        <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Reversibility</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">Normalise where mistakes are reversible; defer normalisation where they're not. A wrong materialized view is a redefinition away from correction. A wrong schema at ingest is a multi-service migration. Applied at the data platform: land raw, fan-out shaped. Applied at segmentation: consolidate first, model at the analytics layer second.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Match storage to question</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">Recommendations want point lookups; segmentation wants population filtering; reporting wants columnar aggregation. One database cannot efficiently answer all three. Choose the storage pattern for the access pattern, not the other way around.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Operational simplicity beats sophisticated abstractions</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">Legible systems are easier to debug than clever ones. A Pub/Sub consumer publishing lag metrics and failing visibly beats a Dataflow job hiding what's actually happening in an execution graph. When a small team owns it, debuggability under pressure beats a better abstraction on paper.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Ship in trust order, not sophistication order</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">Built manual recommendation blocks first (zero intelligence, but deployable day one), then automated, then smart. Clients who started on manual graduated to smart. Sophistication matters less than adoption; adoption requires trust.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Contact CTA -->
  <section style="padding: 52px 0; text-align: center;">
    <p style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 16px;">Let's talk about infrastructure, data, and building at scale.</p>
    <a href="mailto:mail4udhaya@gmail.com" style="text-decoration: none; color: var(--accent); font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 1px solid transparent; transition: border-color 0.2s ease;">mail4udhaya@gmail.com</a>
    <p style="margin-top: 24px;"><a href="/resume">View resume →</a></p>
  </section>
</Layout>
